## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to architect cross-tenant secret governance, rotation, and access governance in a multi-tenant Azure environment, plus rollback strategies.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant Key Vaults plus central SharedKV
- Managed identities for secret access
- 90-day rotation with versioning
- Azure AD B2B and access reviews
- Defender for Cloud/Monitor auditing
- Rollback and failover plans

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: configure 90-day rotation on SharedKV
const { SecretClient } = require("@azure/keyvault-secrets");
const { DefaultAzureCredential } = require("@azure/identity");

const credential = new DefaultAzureCredential();
const client = new SecretClient(vaultUri, credential);

// Set rotation policy
await client.setSecretRotationPolicy(secretName, {
  expiresIn: "P90D",
  notifyInDays: 7
});
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design cross-service, tenant-aware, tamper-resistant logging with strict retention and quick rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Tamper-evident logging; per-tenant key management; HMAC; Key Vault rotation
- Multi-service sinks; Log Analytics and ADLS Gen2 immutable storage
- Real-time integrity checks; Event Hubs; Canary rollout; incident response

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: sign and write log
function signAndWrite(log, tenantId){
  const key = getKeyFromKV(tenantId);
  const signature = hmacSHA256(log, key);
  writeToSink({log, signature, tenantId});
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify integrity without exposing keys?
- How would you handle key compromise and replay attacks?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design end-to-end, production-grade guardrails for cross-tenant deployments in Azure, focusing on identity, secret management, policy gates, canaries, and UEBA automation.

## Key Concepts
- Workload identities and Just-In-Time access
- Azure Key Vault with per-service managed identities
- Azure Policy gates to block secrets in config
- Azure Lighthouse for cross-tenant governance
- Canary deployments with feature flags and automatic rollback
- UEBA via Azure Sentinel with automated playbooks

## Code Example
```json
{
  "policyRule": {
    "if": {
      "field": "type",
      "in": ["Microsoft.Web/sites", "Microsoft.AzureFunctionsJobHost"]
    },
    "then": {
      "effect": "auditIfNotExists",
      "details": {
        "type": "Microsoft.KeyVault/vaults/secrets"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
